```java
    public static void main(String[] args){

        Observable<Integer> i = Observable.create((ObservableEmitter<Integer> e) -> {
            throw new RuntimeException("h1");
        }).subscribeOn(Schedulers.io());

        Observable<Integer> i2 = Observable.create((ObservableEmitter<Integer> e) -> {
            throw new RuntimeException("h2");
        }).subscribeOn(Schedulers.io());

        Observable.merge(i, i2)
                .subscribeOn(Schedulers.io())
                .subscribe(
                        integer -> {
                            System.out.println("integer = " + integer);
                        },
                        throwable -> {
                            System.out.println("throwable = " + throwable);
                        });

        try {
            Thread.sleep(20 * 1000);
        } catch (InterruptedException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
```

If I remove `i`, `i2` subscribeOn operator. It works fine.


